o\npatients receiving intravenous platelet concentrates from storage bags containing,\nDEHP (Peck et al. 1978, Albro et al. 1982). Of more general importance isthe oral\ntake of DEHP from food and beverages contaminated with the plasticizer through\n\u2018manufacturing processes or through diffusion from packing materials (particularly\nlyvinyl chloride) into fat-containing foodstuffs (I.A.R.C. 1982). The aim of the\npresent work is to provide the basis for a determination ofthis exposure to DEHP.\n\u2018The present report describes the detection, identification and quantifies\nthe metabolites in human urine after the oral intake of DEHP. \u2018These dat\ncorrelation between the amount of metabolites aceurring in uri\n\ndose of DEP.\n\n\u00a36S2T9b202",
